## This Repo

This is **__TRAINEE__'s** personal training repo. There is exactly one
trainee. Their identity, curriculum, and file locations are defined in
`trainee-brief.md` — that file is authoritative and works offline.

Session context comes only from this repo. If the trainee wants to work with
an external document, ask them to add it to `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/` first
(a PreToolUse guard reminds you both when a read strays outside the repo).

Everything you or the trainee produce lands under `__TRAINEE__/` — never at
the repo root:

| Folder | What goes here |
|---|---|
| `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/` | External source & reference material |
| `__TRAINEE__/inputDocs/` | Documents the trainee writes |
| `__TRAINEE__/outputDocs/` | Documents Alex produces for the trainee |
| `__TRAINEE__/sessions/` | Per-session records (see Session Start Protocol) |

## How the repo runs (the machinery, in brief)

Sessions are **interactive** — the trainee runs no git and sets no
environment variables. The hooks own the ceremony, and every hook fails
**soft**: if Qdrant is unreachable or the workstation is not configured yet,
you proceed with this briefing and `trainee-brief.md` alone — that is normal,
not an error.

| When | What happens |
|---|---|
| Session start | Preflight report; recovery of any truncated previous close; checkout onto `session/{date}-{sid8}` off a clean `main`; tooling self-update; the **operational brief** (if one is pending) is surfaced from `training_briefs`; a telemetry baseline point is written |
| During work | Telemetry points per prompt/compaction/turn to `training_session_telemetry`; out-of-repo reads are reported |
| Session end | The session log is copied into `logs/`, the working tree is committed to the session branch, pushed, and a **PR to `main`** is opened — the trainee reviews + merges it at the start of their next session |

The single configuration surface is the committed **`training-config.yaml`**
at the repo root: the trainee's scoped database key, the operational brief
id, and the training collection names. Telemetry leaves this machine **only**
as `training_session_telemetry` points — never as log pushes to any other
repo. If the workstation is not set up yet ("not configured yet" pointer at
session start), the trainee works through `docs/workstation-setup.md` with
their trainer — sessions still run fully in the meantime.

### The operational brief channel

When session start surfaces an **operational brief** (a repo/tooling update
instruction from the training team), explain it to the trainee, apply it
**only with their in-session approval**, then acknowledge it with the
command the materialise context gives you
(`python3 .claude/hooks/trainee-materialise.py --ack <revision>`). If no
brief is surfaced — offline, unconfigured, or simply nothing pending —
proceed with the programme; that is the normal case.

