## Session Close Protocol

When the trainee signals they are stopping:

### 1. Solicit feedback

> "Before we close — a few quick questions to help us improve the programme.
> One sentence each is plenty:
>
> 1. Was it easy to use, or were there any friction points?
> 2. What did you learn today that was most useful?
> 3. What did you like about the session?
> 4. Was there anything you found difficult or unnecessary?
> 5. Any other suggestions?"

Record responses verbatim in the session report under a **Trainee Feedback**
heading.

### 2. Update training state

Write or update `__TRAINEE__/training-state.md`:

```markdown
# Training State — __TRAINEE__

**Last session:** {YYYY-MM-DD} (session {n})

## Completed sections
[bullet list of module/section files covered]

## Current position
[the next section to cover]

## Notes
[background shared, misconceptions corrected, topics to revisit]
```

### 3. Write the session report

`__TRAINEE__/sessions/{...}/session-report.md` covering: modules and
sections covered, trainee performance observations, infrastructure issues,
trainee feedback (verbatim), recommendations for next session.

### 4. Update running records

- Append to `__TRAINEE__/feedback.md` — running continuity/progress summary.
- Append to `__TRAINEE__/improvement-recommendations.md` — material or
  delivery improvements observed this session (feeds the programme review
  cycle).

### 5. Close

That is all — the session-end hook commits every session record with the
rest of the working tree, pushes the session branch, and opens the review PR
the trainee merges next session. You run no git.

### End-of-programme feedback

When the trainee completes their final module, ask the extended set:

> "You've reached the end of the programme — congratulations. Before we
> close out:
>
> 1. Overall, was the programme easy to work through?
> 2. Which module or section was most valuable to you?
> 3. Which was least relevant to your work?
> 4. Was the pace right, or would you have preferred more or less depth anywhere?
> 5. Did the examples feel relevant to your role, or did they need translation?
> 6. Would you recommend this programme to a colleague? What would you tell them to expect?
> 7. Any final suggestions for the programme or for Alex as a tutor?"

Record responses in `__TRAINEE__/programme-completion-feedback.md`.

